From a21ec90a5b1faf6448a7daec2d70acb15e647692 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakr <git@qaq.wiki>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 05:28:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 09/24] Lift a quarantine only for a disjoint new incarnation,
 after its checks

Two gaps left in the lift.

The lift ran before the adopted table's collision checks. A new table
that still collided with another mapping lifted the quarantine and
dropped the frame first, and only then failed and quarantined again, the
frame already gone. The lift now runs at the end of a resolve whose table
passed every check; a table that fails returns before it can lift or drop
anything.

Any table change after a MAP counted as a new backing, so a late MAP left
a standing permission that a filled hole, a shortened list, a changed
invalid entry or one changed page then cashed in for the whole window.
None of those says the old pages are owned again. The lift now takes a
new MappingInternal for the id since the quarantine whose adopted table
has valid pages and shares none with the quarantined table; a MAP alone
never lifts, and without that evidence the mapping stays quarantined.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit c445e36079d45a650a4dbd573fc7fb67e5d3e8ba)
